 57: 
 58: ### Root Cause Analysis
 59: 1. **Container Scrolled Out of View**: The WebGL container `<div ref={mountRef}>` was styled with `absolute inset-0` inside the `<section id="hero">`. When the user scrolled past the hero section, the entire container scrolled off-screen.
 60: 2. **Excessive Vertical Drop Formula**: `cascadeDropY` was set to `dropEased * 10.5`. In Three.js units with camera at $Z \approx 7.8$, a drop of 10.5 plunged the cards completely below the camera's bottom frustum boundary ($Y \approx -3.2$).
 61: 3. **Local Mouse Tracking Scope**: Pointer move listener was attached to `#hero`, preventing cursor updates once scrolled into other sections.
 62: 4. **Opaque Scene Background & Atmospheric Overlay**: Three.js had solid black `scene.background = new THREE.Color("#120E15")` and an 88% dark bottom gradient blocking visibility.
