263:    - Removed `destScale = 0.001` and $Z \to -16$ recession code completely across all cards in [HeroSection.tsx](file:///f:/C++/codes/Hackathons/Saskaran%20deck%20of%20cards%202026%20static%20site/src/components/event/HeroSection.tsx).
264:    - Preserved full physical scale ($1.05\times$ scale) on all 18 procedural cards throughout the entire scroll journey.
265: 2. **Continuous Vertical Parallax Formula**:
266:    - Each card $i$ is assigned a staggered vertical base ($Y = ((i \% 6) - 2.5) \times 2.4$) and a differential layer speed ($2.4$ to $4.5\times$).
267:    - As $scroll$ progresses, cards drift smoothly upward along $Y$ (`verticalParallaxY = verticalBaseY + scroll * parallaxSpeed * 2.2`), creating a continuous cinematic tracking motion.
268: 3. **Gutter Flanking**:
269:    - Cards smoothly fan out to flank the left ($X \approx -3.1$ to $-4.5$) and right ($X \approx +3.1$ to $+4.5$) gutters as the user scrolls away from the hero, keeping the central reading column completely clear for content.
270: 4. **Cinematic Rotational Sway & Depth**:
271:    - Layered $Z$-depths ($Z \approx +1.8$ to $-6.5$) with natural perspective.
272:    - Rotational roll ($Z$) and pitch ($X$) sway with phase offsets, plus global mouse cursor parallax tracking.
273: 5. **Vertical Camera Tracking**:
274:    - Added subtle vertical camera descent and lookAt tracking ($scrollCamY = -scroll \times 0.8$), deepening the filmic perspective.
